openslide-js-1.0.0-beta.5: the browser build of @computationalpathologygroup/openslide-js
1.0.0-beta.5 (npm, dist-tag "beta", published 2026-07-02 with an npm provenance attestation),
OpenSlide 4.0.0 compiled to WebAssembly. The website's page reads whole-slide images with it
(MRXS, NDPI, SVS, Sakura; client/src/js/node/slideReader.js); the desktop app never loads it.

These files are the package's dist/esm runtime, unchanged, byte for byte: the ES module wrapper,
its worker (worker.js, bundled by the package), the Emscripten glue (wasm/openslide.js) and the
WebAssembly binary (wasm/openslide.wasm). The package's source maps, TypeScript declarations,
CommonJS build, single-file variant and bundler helpers are left out. The wasm is loaded at run
time as its own file; nothing of it is linked into Plexora's code.

Licence: LGPL-2.1-only (LICENSE, the package's own; NOTICE lists every component statically linked
into openslide.wasm and its licence: OpenSlide, GLib, Cairo and gdk-pixbuf under the LGPL; the rest
MIT, BSD, zlib, libpng, IJG, FTL or public domain).

Corresponding source (LGPL-2.1 section 6): https://github.com/computationalpathologygroup/openslide-js,
at the commit 1.0.0-beta.5 was built from (npm gitHead dff6ab5cf7fc0d55e0c5732a227e221c203ab26a),
whose wasm/ directory
holds the Dockerfile, the pinned fetch script for every bundled project and every patch applied.
